WEBVTT

00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:25.526
I know!

00:00:25.526 --> 00:00:28.654
Kakei must have an
unexpectedly unkempt side.

00:00:28.654 --> 00:00:33.325
Wouldn't he be attracted to the type
that goes all out with tender, loving care?

00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:36.328
Maybe he likes girls who are good at cooking?

00:00:36.328 --> 00:00:41.625
He said something about how girls who can
make good meat and potato stew are nice...

00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:45.754
Kakei's cool and aloof,
so maybe he likes the same type of girl?

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:48.674
No, no, no. He likes joking around,

00:00:48.674 --> 00:00:51.343
so he might like girls who don't
mind being the butt of his jokes...

00:00:52.928 --> 00:00:54.888
We aren't making any progress...

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:58.600
Anyway, I thought Kakei
was going out with Koda--

00:01:00.018 --> 00:01:03.480
It's true that he is often with Kodachi...

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.233
But they don't look like they're dating.

00:01:06.233 --> 00:01:08.735
I guess we'll have to ask Kakei after all...

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:13.115
No, we can't! We can't let
Kakei find out about this.

00:01:13.866 --> 00:01:16.660
What about me?

00:01:17.536 --> 00:01:19.246
K-Kakei!

00:01:19.246 --> 00:01:23.208
U-Um, hey, are you free this Sunday?

00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:24.334
Yeah...

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:27.254
Um... If it's all right with you...

00:01:27.254 --> 00:01:30.174
Please go on a date with us!

00:01:30.174 --> 00:01:31.133
Huh?

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.968
What?!

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:46.481
<i>Writing down my aspirations</i>

00:01:46.481 --> 00:01:49.234
<i>For the day when they will come true</i>

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:54.573
<i>The time has come when</i>
<i>I want to turn to the page I marked</i>

00:01:54.573 --> 00:02:00.037
<i>Although there are things I lose</i>
<i>sight of with everything that happens</i>

00:02:00.037 --> 00:02:01.413
<i>Hey, it's all right</i>

00:02:01.413 --> 00:02:05.334
<i>The start I'm embarking on is unexpected</i>

00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:08.170
<i>The memory that you couldn't erase</i>

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.839
<i>Even that sad memory</i>

00:02:10.839 --> 00:02:14.885
<i>I'll give it a different, happier reading</i>

00:02:14.885 --> 00:02:20.516
<i>I feel like just that will change everything</i>

00:02:20.516 --> 00:02:21.642
<i>All Right</i>

00:02:21.642 --> 00:02:24.853
<i>So come now, the way you are!</i>

00:02:24.853 --> 00:02:27.689
<i>Don't hide your weak self</i>

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:28.690
<i>On my Sheep </i>

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:32.361
<i>Let's meet riding on a dream</i>

00:02:32.361 --> 00:02:38.283
<i>Even just calling your name as</i>
<i>I write in this book of adventures</i>

00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:41.119
<i>I'm not lost anymore</i>

00:02:41.119 --> 00:02:44.831
<i>Let's start our journey together</i>

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:52.589
<i>Yes... more of you and me!</i>

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:06.061
"Sunday"

00:03:07.479 --> 00:03:09.231
"Episode 7: The Library Club's Day Off"
Coming, coming.

00:03:09.231 --> 00:03:10.607
"Episode 7: The Library Club's Day Off"

00:03:10.607 --> 00:03:12.359
"Episode 7: The Library Club's Day Off"
You're too noisy, Kodachi.

00:03:12.359 --> 00:03:13.569
I'm Kodachi.

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:14.820
Kodachi here.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:16.405
I'm Kodachi!

00:03:16.405 --> 00:03:18.198
I am Kodachi...

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:21.577
Kakei, what time is it right now?

00:03:22.828 --> 00:03:27.791
Ah, sorry... I was reading until early
this morning, and then I fell asleep...

00:03:27.791 --> 00:03:28.667
Kakei!

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:29.501
Yes?!

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:33.630
Don't you think it's bad to be late for a date?

00:03:35.424 --> 00:03:37.467
Wow...

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:40.762
So this is Kakei's room...

00:03:40.762 --> 00:03:42.723
I'm borrowing your fridge.

00:03:42.723 --> 00:03:44.725
Aren't we going out?

00:03:44.725 --> 00:03:50.480
Yes, we would already <i>be </i>out
right now if you hadn't been late.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.900
Sorry...

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.484
Shirasaki?!

00:03:54.484 --> 00:03:57.487
The dishes in the sink were bothering me.

00:03:57.487 --> 00:03:59.823
It's fine, you don't have to do that.

00:03:59.823 --> 00:04:02.117
It's okay, I'll be done soon.

00:04:02.117 --> 00:04:03.410
Sorry about that...

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:06.830
There... There it is!

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:09.416
<i>Murder in the Mansion of Black Death.</i>

00:04:09.416 --> 00:04:11.251
<i>Dogra Magra.</i>

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:13.003
<i>Offering to Nothingness.</i>

00:04:13.003 --> 00:04:15.672
These are Japan's three
great novels of the bizarre!

00:04:15.672 --> 00:04:18.675
Kakei, you need to shelve your books.

00:04:18.675 --> 00:04:20.552
--My shelves full already.
--Oh, you read these kinds of books, too, Kakei?

00:04:20.552 --> 00:04:22.054
--This is annoying.
--Oh, you read these kinds of books, too, Kakei?

00:04:22.054 --> 00:04:24.723
--They should be lined up neatly!
--Oh, you read these kinds of books, too, Kakei?

00:04:24.723 --> 00:04:27.684
--Does it matter? It's not like you live here...
--I like them, too!

00:04:27.684 --> 00:04:29.686
That might not always be the case.

00:04:29.686 --> 00:04:30.896
Huh?

00:04:30.896 --> 00:04:33.982
Oh, I mean, there's no way I'd live here.

00:04:33.982 --> 00:04:35.651
What the heck am I saying?

00:04:35.651 --> 00:04:37.903
I thought it was a noisy morning...

00:04:37.903 --> 00:04:40.697
What's this, did you all come
to have a beauty contest?

00:04:40.697 --> 00:04:42.407
Why'd you come in without knocking?

00:04:42.407 --> 00:04:45.369
It's fine, isn't it? It's what I always do.

00:04:45.369 --> 00:04:47.412
What you...

00:04:47.412 --> 00:04:48.956
...always do?!

00:04:48.956 --> 00:04:51.625
So you really are neighbors.

00:04:51.625 --> 00:04:55.337
And you're close enough
to come in without asking...

00:04:55.337 --> 00:04:59.383
Aren't we going shopping today?
We should go soon!

00:04:59.383 --> 00:05:02.469
Oh, then I'll go, too!

00:05:02.469 --> 00:05:04.054
What?

00:05:10.769 --> 00:05:13.939
Tamamo, is there a store you like?

00:05:13.939 --> 00:05:17.568
Not really. Do you know of a good place?

00:05:17.568 --> 00:05:21.405
Hmm... A place I go to a lot...

00:05:21.405 --> 00:05:23.240
Here, I guess.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:25.826
It looks like there are
a lot of cute clothes here.

00:05:25.826 --> 00:05:29.288
If I wore something like this,
I would be reported immediately.

00:05:29.288 --> 00:05:34.376
What? But I think they'd
look cute on you. Right, Kakei?

00:05:34.376 --> 00:05:38.130
Yeah, I mean, at the very least,
you wouldn't be reported.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:39.673
I-I guess...

00:05:39.673 --> 00:05:44.761
And so, let's start Sakuraba's makeover now!

00:05:44.761 --> 00:05:46.847
Don't you think this would look good?

00:05:46.847 --> 00:05:48.807
Yeah, that might be nice!

00:05:48.807 --> 00:05:50.434
What do you think, Tamamo?

00:05:50.434 --> 00:05:51.977
Y-Yeah...

00:05:51.977 --> 00:05:54.313
It's scandalously cute...

00:05:54.313 --> 00:05:57.024
I think this would look good, too!

00:05:59.318 --> 00:06:02.446
Four girls at once? Not bad, Kakei.

00:06:02.446 --> 00:06:04.448
We're just shopping.

00:06:04.448 --> 00:06:07.659
Oh? You look like you're having fun, though.

00:06:07.659 --> 00:06:09.703
Really?

00:06:11.705 --> 00:06:13.207
I guess so.

00:06:13.207 --> 00:06:15.501
Well? Who are you <i>really </i>after?

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:16.710
Huh?

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:19.421
It must be nice to have
so many types to choose from.

00:06:19.421 --> 00:06:22.841
Oh, but don't choose all
of them and make a scene.

00:06:22.841 --> 00:06:26.220
I don't want there to be issues next door.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:27.679
Don't even start...

00:06:27.679 --> 00:06:29.223
Kakei.

00:06:34.019 --> 00:06:36.146
How is it? Isn't it cute?

00:06:36.146 --> 00:06:39.233
What?! Y-Yeah...

00:06:44.363 --> 00:06:49.201
What're you doing? You should
at least say, "That's cute, honey."

00:06:49.201 --> 00:06:50.577
Like I could say that!

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:18.689
The next thing on our
schedule is lunch from 11:45.

00:07:18.689 --> 00:07:20.649
That's very specific.

00:07:20.649 --> 00:07:23.068
Did you come up with a schedule for today?

00:07:23.068 --> 00:07:24.653
Of course!

00:07:24.653 --> 00:07:29.074
Well, well... It's a plan for the perfect date.

00:07:29.074 --> 00:07:32.119
I-It's because Shirasaki
was looking forward to it...

00:07:32.119 --> 00:07:34.371
I didn't care either way...

00:07:34.371 --> 00:07:37.666
You looked things up pretty carefully, though.

00:07:37.666 --> 00:07:41.378
Oh! That last place--"The hilly park
where you can see the sunset"--

00:07:41.378 --> 00:07:44.673
It's that spot where everyone confesses
their feelings to their love interest!

00:07:47.176 --> 00:07:50.470
Th-There's no time! Let's hurry!

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:53.015
Aw, there's a long line...

00:07:53.015 --> 00:07:56.977
It's because this place has
been on a lot of food shows.

00:07:56.977 --> 00:07:58.854
We'll just have to line up then!

00:07:58.854 --> 00:08:02.816
No, but if we line up now,
we'll probably have at least an hour wait.

00:08:02.816 --> 00:08:04.484
But...

00:08:05.319 --> 00:08:06.945
I'm sorry!

00:08:06.945 --> 00:08:09.406
I should have made a reservation!

00:08:09.406 --> 00:08:11.450
No, this actually helps me out.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:12.284
Huh?

00:08:12.284 --> 00:08:14.453
Money's kind of tight this month,

00:08:14.453 --> 00:08:17.789
so even though it's sad because
you found a nice restaurant,

00:08:17.789 --> 00:08:20.834
it'd be better for me
to go to a place like that.

00:08:23.253 --> 00:08:24.963
Kakei...

00:08:27.299 --> 00:08:30.219
I need to be more flexible...

00:08:30.219 --> 00:08:33.138
Yes! I can't be so uncompromising.

00:08:33.138 --> 00:08:34.264
Yeah!

00:08:34.264 --> 00:08:37.559
They're good for each other,
aren't they? Kakei and Tamamo.

00:08:37.559 --> 00:08:41.605
He gets points for covering for her so smoothly.

00:08:41.605 --> 00:08:44.691
But they're less like lovers
and more like partners.

00:09:03.919 --> 00:09:04.837
"Arcade"

00:09:04.837 --> 00:09:08.423
Hey, will someone play me?

00:09:08.423 --> 00:09:09.925
I accept your challenge!

00:09:09.925 --> 00:09:12.052
You play these things, Misono?

00:09:12.052 --> 00:09:16.306
No, it's my first time, but I train every day.

00:09:18.392 --> 00:09:20.602
Go, Senri!

00:09:30.279 --> 00:09:32.239
Misono's amazing!

00:09:32.239 --> 00:09:35.242
Yeah, but...

00:09:37.744 --> 00:09:40.163
I don't know where to look...

00:09:40.163 --> 00:09:42.332
Must be nice to move so easily.

00:09:42.332 --> 00:09:46.461
I've got these extra weights, you know...

00:09:52.718 --> 00:09:56.346
Oh, they're good!
They've got pretty high scores!

00:10:12.279 --> 00:10:13.655
Does it hurt?

00:10:13.655 --> 00:10:14.907
No.

00:10:14.907 --> 00:10:21.496
Anyway, from here, you look like a
pervert who was ordered to lick my feet.

00:10:21.496 --> 00:10:24.416
If you can joke around, you must be fine.

00:10:24.416 --> 00:10:26.668
Sorry to make you worry...

00:10:27.628 --> 00:10:28.921
Kakei.

00:10:28.921 --> 00:10:29.838
Hm?

00:10:29.838 --> 00:10:32.382
Have you ever been in one of those?

00:10:32.382 --> 00:10:34.301
No, never.

00:10:34.301 --> 00:10:36.053
Me neither.

00:10:36.053 --> 00:10:39.181
Which means, it'd be
both of our first times, huh?

00:10:39.181 --> 00:10:41.141
1,000,000 volts!

00:10:41.975 --> 00:10:44.228
Kakei, please get closer.

00:10:44.228 --> 00:10:45.979
H-Hey.

00:10:45.979 --> 00:10:48.357
Oh, are you embarrassed?

00:10:48.357 --> 00:10:50.567
I <i>am </i>a guy, you know.

00:10:50.567 --> 00:10:53.695
Speaking of which, I heard from a friend

00:10:53.695 --> 00:10:58.116
that since this is closed room,
there are couples who kiss in here.

00:10:58.116 --> 00:10:59.660
Huh?!

00:11:02.871 --> 00:11:04.790
Thanks for making a good face.

00:11:06.542 --> 00:11:08.877
A girl like Senri that
you just can't leave alone

00:11:08.877 --> 00:11:12.422
might be what someone with
Kakei's personality is looking for.

00:11:12.422 --> 00:11:16.635
It looks more like Misono is
having fun teasing Kakei, though...

00:11:20.138 --> 00:11:21.932
"Factory Photo Book"
I've been looking for this for forever!

00:11:21.932 --> 00:11:23.642
A factory photo book!

00:11:23.642 --> 00:11:26.478
Kanasuke, are you someone
who likes eccentric things?

00:11:26.478 --> 00:11:30.148
No, I know other people who like what I like.

00:11:31.066 --> 00:11:34.069
Wait, Kakei, are you buying <i>all </i>of those?

00:11:34.069 --> 00:11:36.530
I thought you said money was tight this month?

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:40.492
Yeah, that's why it was
hard to narrow them down...

00:11:40.492 --> 00:11:44.746
Wow, you've got all sorts
of different genres there.

00:11:44.746 --> 00:11:48.000
Kakei, do you read indiscriminately?

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.252
Well, I guess I'll read anything...

00:11:50.252 --> 00:11:54.923
Then, are there any
books you would recommend?

00:11:54.923 --> 00:11:58.552
What kinds of books do you like, Kanasuke?

00:11:58.552 --> 00:12:00.512
This is kinda nice.

00:12:00.512 --> 00:12:01.680
Hm?

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:06.518
This is the first time I've talked
about books this much with a boy.

00:12:06.518 --> 00:12:08.937
It's important to be able to share hobbies, huh?

00:12:08.937 --> 00:12:12.524
And Kakei always looks like
he's having fun when he's with Kana.

00:12:12.524 --> 00:12:15.235
That's true. They do make a good pair.

00:12:15.235 --> 00:12:16.236
"Mystery"

00:12:16.236 --> 00:12:17.571
Speaking of which...

00:12:17.571 --> 00:12:18.530
Hm?

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:22.701
What happened with the
bet you had on the Library Club?

00:12:22.701 --> 00:12:25.329
I can't believe you remember that.

00:12:25.329 --> 00:12:27.956
It sounded like it was important.

00:12:27.956 --> 00:12:29.541
Yeah, well...

00:12:29.541 --> 00:12:31.710
I did win the bet.

00:12:33.921 --> 00:12:36.173
Oh, are you looking at me?

00:12:36.173 --> 00:12:39.343
Don't worry about it. It's just a habit.

00:12:39.343 --> 00:12:43.597
I can't... If someone I think
is special looks at me that way...

00:12:44.598 --> 00:12:46.141
Just kidding!

00:12:46.141 --> 00:12:48.060
Did your heart skip a beat?

00:12:49.144 --> 00:12:53.524
"Do you know your true self?"

00:12:54.274 --> 00:12:56.693
That definitely tired me out.

00:12:56.693 --> 00:12:58.278
Shall we take a break?

00:12:58.278 --> 00:13:00.948
Yeah, I think there was
a food court around here...

00:13:00.948 --> 00:13:03.909
Okay, your fun date ends here.

00:13:03.909 --> 00:13:07.037
Now, it's time to do Shepherd work.

00:13:13.043 --> 00:13:17.130
Shirasaki's fate is about to change greatly...

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:18.715
Shirasaki's?!

00:13:18.715 --> 00:13:21.760
Now, let's start the mission!

00:13:29.726 --> 00:13:33.397
I see, so that's how it is.

00:13:33.397 --> 00:13:41.947
The man in this book is an artist likely
to create many history-making pieces.

00:13:41.947 --> 00:13:44.449
But through his meeting
with Shirasaki in the near future,

00:13:44.449 --> 00:13:48.036
his fate will veer greatly off-course.

00:13:48.036 --> 00:13:51.540
Falling in love with Shirasaki at
first sight, he will confess his feelings,

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.959
and despite being turned down gently,

00:13:53.959 --> 00:13:57.754
he won't give up and will
continue to attack many times.

00:13:57.754 --> 00:13:59.298
In the end...

00:13:59.298 --> 00:14:01.675
Don't tell me he turns into a stalker?

00:14:01.675 --> 00:14:06.180
No, it looks like he
gives up on Shirasaki, but...

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:08.098
Here...

00:14:12.769 --> 00:14:20.152
It says he will use all the overflowing
talent he has to perfect an elaborate love doll.

00:14:20.152 --> 00:14:21.361
And the name of that doll is...

00:14:21.361 --> 00:14:24.615
Tsugumi #18!

00:14:24.615 --> 00:14:25.908
Huh?

00:14:25.908 --> 00:14:29.244
Tsugumi #18 will be a big hit worldwide!

00:14:29.244 --> 00:14:35.959
And Shirasaki's name will be carved
into history as the model for Tsugumi #18...

00:14:37.461 --> 00:14:40.047
Is this such a bad future?

00:14:40.047 --> 00:14:40.881
What?

00:14:40.881 --> 00:14:44.009
From the looks of it,
it's a very well made doll...

00:14:44.009 --> 00:14:47.012
What's a "love doll," anyway?

00:14:47.012 --> 00:14:48.972
Well, it's...

00:14:54.186 --> 00:14:56.396
Wh-What the hell? I can't believe it!

00:14:56.396 --> 00:14:58.357
I can't believe it's used for <i>that</i>!

00:14:58.357 --> 00:15:00.025
Just how perverted can you be?!

00:15:00.025 --> 00:15:02.986
Even if you ask <i>me </i>that...

00:15:02.986 --> 00:15:04.446
Oh!

00:15:07.032 --> 00:15:08.951
The target's here!

00:15:10.827 --> 00:15:12.079
What should we do?

00:15:12.079 --> 00:15:14.081
At this rate, it's just a matter of time!

00:15:14.081 --> 00:15:15.999
Kakei, I'm leaving it to you!

00:15:15.999 --> 00:15:18.585
Huh? What do you want me to do?

00:15:18.585 --> 00:15:20.462
For now, just...

00:15:24.258 --> 00:15:25.467
What?!

00:15:31.974 --> 00:15:33.141
Shirasaki...

00:15:33.141 --> 00:15:36.103
Oh, Kakei, over here!

00:15:40.148 --> 00:15:44.903
You look cute today, too... my honey, Tsugumi.

00:15:45.904 --> 00:15:50.409
Huh? What? Kakei... What?

00:15:50.409 --> 00:15:54.413
Tsugumi, can I hold you tighter?

00:15:55.539 --> 00:15:57.374
Kakei...

00:16:04.298 --> 00:16:05.716
Excuse me!

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:20.731
I hope he and Shirasaki's lives
will go in a better direction now...

00:16:20.731 --> 00:16:22.691
Um, Kakei!

00:16:24.151 --> 00:16:25.777
What in the world are you doing?

00:16:25.777 --> 00:16:28.572
Kakei! What's all the commotion?

00:16:28.572 --> 00:16:31.700
I-It's... There's a very good reason for this...

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:33.785
Shirasaki, please let me explain!

00:16:37.539 --> 00:16:39.833
You arranged this together, Kodachi?!

00:16:39.833 --> 00:16:43.712
Yeah, 'cause you guys seemed like
you were hiding something from Kakei.

00:16:43.712 --> 00:16:45.130
Oh...

00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:49.635
So we thought we'd try something
and see your reaction... Right?

00:16:49.635 --> 00:16:50.594
Yeah...

00:16:50.594 --> 00:16:53.222
Why are you saying this out of the blue?

00:16:53.222 --> 00:16:57.559
Yeah, we're not hiding anything...
are we, Big Sister?

00:16:57.559 --> 00:17:00.270
Th-That's right...

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:04.983
O-Oh my, I would never lie to Kakei...

00:17:04.983 --> 00:17:07.569
Shirasaki... You're making it too obvious.

00:17:07.569 --> 00:17:08.529
Huh?

00:17:08.529 --> 00:17:12.241
Now I know <i>you </i>can't lie at least.

00:17:12.241 --> 00:17:13.242
What?!

00:17:13.242 --> 00:17:16.828
We have no choice.
Let's tell Kakei everything...

00:17:16.828 --> 00:17:18.330
Yeah...

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:19.748
Actually...

00:17:20.499 --> 00:17:22.709
You want to know what type of girl I like?

00:17:22.709 --> 00:17:23.126
"Subject: Kakei from the Library Club"

00:17:23.126 --> 00:17:23.961
"Subject: Kakei from the Library Club"
Yes, we got this...

00:17:23.961 --> 00:17:25.796
"I like Kakei."
Yes, we got this...

00:17:25.796 --> 00:17:29.466
"Will you tell me what type of girl he likes?"
But we didn't know the type of girl you liked,

00:17:29.466 --> 00:17:33.262
so we thought about who you'd
like from among the four of us...

00:17:33.262 --> 00:17:36.223
Isn't this anonymous?
It was probably just a prank...

00:17:36.223 --> 00:17:39.059
Must be nice to have a group date...

00:17:39.059 --> 00:17:46.066
What's with this one poor
club member who wasn't invited, though?

00:17:46.066 --> 00:17:48.026
Don't cry, boy.

00:17:48.026 --> 00:17:49.361
Master Giza...

00:17:49.361 --> 00:17:53.782
You're the only one
who understands how I feel...

00:17:53.782 --> 00:17:54.616
Gross!

00:17:54.616 --> 00:17:56.285
You've been rejected...

00:17:56.285 --> 00:17:56.994
Huh?

00:17:56.994 --> 00:18:00.497
Hm? A section to gather
information about the Shepherd?

00:18:00.497 --> 00:18:02.791
When did we make something like that?

00:18:02.791 --> 00:18:05.836
Huh? What are you saying?
We've had it for a while...

00:18:05.836 --> 00:18:07.921
Now that you mention it...

00:18:07.921 --> 00:18:09.047
Sakuraba?

00:18:09.047 --> 00:18:12.676
I can't remember why we
started something like this.

00:18:12.676 --> 00:18:13.886
Huh...?

00:18:13.886 --> 00:18:15.846
Does anyone have any idea?

00:18:15.846 --> 00:18:16.763
No...

00:18:16.763 --> 00:18:17.723
Nothing.

00:18:17.723 --> 00:18:19.600
I wonder why?

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:23.187
What about you, Kakei? Any ideas?

00:18:23.187 --> 00:18:26.773
We got messages from
the Shepherd, remember?

00:18:26.773 --> 00:18:31.028
And then we tried to uncover the truth
behind who the Shepherd really was...

00:18:31.361 --> 00:18:33.447
Oh, that was it.

00:18:33.447 --> 00:18:35.407
I wonder why we forgot...

00:18:35.407 --> 00:18:38.535
Must be getting old...

00:18:38.535 --> 00:18:41.663
Is that how it is?

00:18:44.499 --> 00:18:50.964
"I like Kakei. Will you tell
me what type of girl he likes?"

00:18:50.964 --> 00:18:52.674
What's going on?

00:18:52.674 --> 00:18:56.011
I was just trying to make you happy.

00:18:56.011 --> 00:18:59.473
I even sent an email asking for
advice to set things up for you,

00:18:59.473 --> 00:19:00.766
but you didn't take advantage of it...

00:19:00.766 --> 00:19:03.477
Not that!

00:19:03.477 --> 00:19:07.648
If I become a Shepherd too,
will everyone forget about me?

00:19:07.648 --> 00:19:12.486
Oh, you're talking about that?
Took you long enough to figure it out.

00:19:12.486 --> 00:19:16.073
When we went to the magic library,
remember what we talked about?

00:19:16.073 --> 00:19:20.452
About how everyone has their own
"book" that has their life written in it.

00:19:20.452 --> 00:19:22.162
Yeah...

00:19:22.162 --> 00:19:25.123
Shepherds don't have books.

00:19:26.416 --> 00:19:31.505
More precisely, these books that are proof
of their existence as humans become erased

00:19:31.505 --> 00:19:35.175
when they become Shepherds.

00:19:35.175 --> 00:19:40.264
That's why Shepherds don't remain
in human memories or have life spans.

00:19:40.264 --> 00:19:41.515
In other words,

00:19:41.515 --> 00:19:44.476
they transcend the existence known as humans.

00:19:45.477 --> 00:19:49.815
Did you imagine that you
could have fun with your friends,

00:19:49.815 --> 00:19:54.361
and then work behind the scenes as
a Shepherd for the sake of the world

00:19:54.361 --> 00:19:57.239
and its people?

00:19:57.239 --> 00:19:58.490
Are you stupid?

00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:04.663
This world isn't so accommodating as
to give you such great power for free!

00:20:04.663 --> 00:20:08.375
Well, do you still want to become a Shepherd?

00:20:08.375 --> 00:20:11.962
To the point where you'd erase your
time with Shirasaki and the others?

00:20:14.965 --> 00:20:17.509
I heard the amusement park is really fun!

00:20:17.509 --> 00:20:20.345
Oh really? I want to go!

00:20:20.345 --> 00:20:21.638
Why don't we go together?

00:20:21.638 --> 00:20:24.308
--I'm sure it'll be fun with everyone!
--Then, what about next Sunday?

00:20:24.308 --> 00:20:28.020
--Oh, that sounds good! I'm free!
--I'm free, too!

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:29.605
--Let's ride a bunch of fast roller coasters!
--Yeah!

00:20:29.605 --> 00:20:31.815
No way...

00:20:31.815 --> 00:20:36.737
When did I start thinking
I didn't want to give them up...?

00:20:37.863 --> 00:20:43.035
Well, if you're going to withdraw from
the Shepherd test, you should do it soon.

00:20:43.869 --> 00:20:45.495
Are <i>you </i>okay with it?

00:20:45.495 --> 00:20:47.080
With what?

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:51.627
With becoming a Shepherd and being
erased from everyone's memories...

00:20:51.627 --> 00:20:56.757
I want to become a Shepherd and
guide the world to a better place.

00:20:56.757 --> 00:21:00.636
To do that, I have resolved to
give up anything and everything.

00:21:00.636 --> 00:21:03.013
I see...

00:21:03.013 --> 00:21:06.600
Then even I'll forget about you...

00:21:09.269 --> 00:21:11.188
That's right...

00:21:11.188 --> 00:21:15.359
You will forget about me...

00:21:34.169 --> 00:21:38.715
You'll completely forget that we did this!

00:21:39.716 --> 00:21:41.051
Kodachi!

00:21:42.469 --> 00:21:45.305
I have given up everything already.

00:21:51.228 --> 00:21:59.987
<i>The starting bell, the sound of a lock</i>

00:21:59.987 --> 00:22:07.661
<i>While drifting aimlessly, I become an adult</i>

00:22:07.661 --> 00:22:17.504
<i>The time has come when days spent</i>
<i>running and playing seem far away</i>

00:22:17.504 --> 00:22:21.758
<i>The answer I gave here</i>

00:22:21.758 --> 00:22:34.688
<i>Oh, if only it had been</i>
<i>passed down somewhere</i>

00:22:34.688 --> 00:22:39.484
<i>For those crowds walking around lost</i>

00:22:39.484 --> 00:22:43.822
<i>It can be a light that shines on them</i>

00:22:43.822 --> 00:22:52.122
<i>On the other side of the</i>
<i>green belt that surrounds us</i>

00:22:52.122 --> 00:23:00.506
<i>You head toward endless tomorrows</i>

00:23:12.809 --> 00:23:19.483
Hear ye, hear ye, regarding my
unkind treatment in the Library Club!

00:23:19.483 --> 00:23:22.110
Even though I was a founding
member of the Library Club,

00:23:22.110 --> 00:23:24.863
I have recently been treated like I'm not there!

00:23:24.863 --> 00:23:29.326
As a result, I was not even invited
to the group date on our day off!

00:23:29.326 --> 00:23:31.453
What is the reason for my existence?!

00:23:31.453 --> 00:23:34.957
Oh, Takamine. Can you get
the box on the shelf for me?

00:23:34.957 --> 00:23:37.088
"Next time: The Magic Book"
With pleasure!
